# Frontend build-time configuration (Vite). Copy to `.env` if needed —
# real `.env` files are gitignored; this example is the tracked template.
#
# VITE_APP_ENV — the bundle's COMPILED-IN environment identity
# (development | staging | production). Leave unset for local development:
# unset builds carry the development identity, the mock/demo data layer,
# and the environment banner. CI and the deploy workflows set this via the
# process environment (which overrides .env files); production bundles are
# built only by the release/installer paths.
# VITE_APP_ENV=development
#
# There is NO API-base env var. The API base is resolved at RUNTIME from
# /runtime-config.js (see public/runtime-config.js and
# src/lib/runtimeConfig.ts): '' = same-origin, an absolute URL =
# cross-origin (the Pages deploy overwrites the file), null = the no-API
# mock demo. Production bundles ignore it entirely — they are same-origin
# by construction and carry no hostname. VITE_API_BASE_URL is RETIRED
# (appliance Phase 1) and no longer read anywhere.
#
# Server-side configuration (APP_ENV, DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET, …) is
# process-environment / aurora.env territory — never a frontend .env file.
